{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_006","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"Title: LBV phenomenon and binarity: The environment of HR Car","location_hint":"paragraph 18","char_start":832,"char_end":893,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_007","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"Authors: A. Mehner , S. Janssens , C. Agliozzo , W.-J. de Wit , H. M. J. Boffin , D. Baade , J. Bodensteiner , J. H. Groh , L. Mahy , F. P. A. Vogt","location_hint":"paragraph 19","char_start":897,"char_end":1044,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_008","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"View a PDF of the paper titled LBV phenomenon and binarity: The environment of HR Car, by A. Mehner and 9 other authors","location_hint":"paragraph 20","char_start":1048,"char_end":1167,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_009","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"Abstract: Luminous blue variable stars (LBVs) are of great interest in massive-star evolution as they experience very high mass-loss episodes within short periods of time.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1181,"char_end":1352,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_010","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"HR Car is a famous member of this class in the Galaxy.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1353,"char_end":1407,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_011","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"It has a large circumstellar nebula and has also been confirmed as being in a binary system.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1408,"char_end":1500,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_012","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"One means of gaining information about the evolutionary status and physical nature of LBVs is studying their environments.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1501,"char_end":1623,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_013","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"We investigated the stellar content within ~100 pc of HR Car and also its circumstellar nebula.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1624,"char_end":1719,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_014","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"Very Large Telescope (VLT) Multi Unit Spectroscopic Explorer (MUSE) observations of a 2'x2' region around the star highlight the incompleteness of stellar classification for stars with magnitudes of V > 13 mag.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1720,"char_end":1930,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_015","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"Eight B0 to B9 stars have been identified which may lie in close spatial vicinity to HR Car.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1931,"char_end":2023,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_016","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"For a region with a radius of r =1.2 degree (~100 pc at a distance of 4.8 kpc) around HR Car, existing catalogs list several late O-type and early B-type stars, but only one early O-type star.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2024,"char_end":2216,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_017","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"Given the relatively low stellar and nebular masses in the HR Car system, no early O-type stars and only a few late O-type stars would be expected in association with HR Car.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2217,"char_end":2391,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_018","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"Instead, HR Car's location in a point vector diagram suggests that HR Car is not isolated, but is part of a moving group with a population of B-type stars in a spiral arm, and it has not received a strong kick from a supernova explosion of a companion star or a merger event.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2392,"char_end":2667,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_019","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"Potential binary evolution pathways for the HR Car system cannot be fully explored because of the unknown nature of the companion star.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2668,"char_end":2803,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_020","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"Furthermore, the MUSE observations reveal the presence of a fast outflow and &#34;bullets&#34; that have been ejected at intervals of about 400 years.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2804,"char_end":2954,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_021","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"These features may have been caused by recurrent mass transfer in the system.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2955,"char_end":3032,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_a2f17fd8c9a6_022","source_id":"src_a2f17fd8c9a6","source_hash":"0ab14ff5f3e04a0499306330319f64d8fc3d762f339261908af7048fd92fa30b","text":"Comments:\n11 pages, 5 figures, to be published in A&A","location_hint":"paragraph 23","char_start":3042,"char_end":3095,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:13.048Z"}
